    "summary": "Girth-strap for horse made of sturdy cotton cloth woven in single width with natural-coloured warp and weft, decorated with central warp patterns in yellow-brown-dyed cotton and some green-dyed cotton. Cloth has tassels at both ends. Two iron rings attached to strap near one end by leather pieces, one natural-coloured, one dyed black; both have red-dyed leather stitching to secure to strap. Other end has large iron ring attached by natural-coloured leather piece to end of strap by red-dyed leather stitching.",
